\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. MINE eyes have seen the glory of 
\par the coming of the Lord :
\par He is trampling out the vintage 
\par where the grapes of wrath are stored ;
\par He hath loosed the fateful lightning 
\par of His terrible swift sword:
\par His truth is marching on.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He hath sounded forth the trumpet 
\par that shall never call retreat ;
\par He is sifting out the hearts of men 
\par before His judgement-seat :
\par O be swift, my soul, to answer Him;
\par be jubilant, my feet!
\par Our God is marching on. 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In the beauty of the lilies Christ 
\par was born across the sea,
\par With a glory in His bosom that 
\par transfigures you and me :
\par As He died to make men holy, 
\par let us live to make men free,
\par While God is marching on.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

